WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:04.609
This is Alabasta, one of the most iconic Islands
in One Piece.

00:00:04.609 --> 00:00:10.549
And this is Cairo, the capital of Egypt, The
ancient temple of Edfu, the gambling city

00:00:10.549 --> 00:00:15.980
of Las Vegas in the United States, traditional
architechture form Mali in west Africa, the

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:19.530
Mehrangarh Fort in India and even the Taj
Mahal.

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:25.020
The epic landmarks and beautiful landscapes
of 4 incredibly different countries from all

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:31.220
around the world, merged into one fantastic
island on the grand line with its own unique

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:33.190
history, culture and people.

00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:36.980
I can't stress enough how impressive I find
this.

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:41.800
Alabasta is a desert kingdom located halfway
through the first part of the grand line with

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:52.329
a history dating back to the infamous void
century 900 years ago.

00:00:52.329 --> 00:00:57.319
At first glance the island seems to be purely
inspired by Egypt, with pyramids and deserts.

00:00:57.319 --> 00:01:02.069
But once I looked a little closer, it became
clear, that there is so much more going on

00:01:02.069 --> 00:01:03.069
here.

00:01:03.069 --> 00:01:07.430
Rain Dinners, the large Casino run by Crocodile,
is a condensed version of the Luxor hotel

00:01:07.430 --> 00:01:08.430
in Vegas.

00:01:08.430 --> 00:01:14.480
The main palace is inspired by India's most
famous landmark, but the roofs have been replaced

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:20.650
with the golden ones of the so-called dome
of the rock, an islamic shrine located in

00:01:20.650 --> 00:01:21.650
Jerusalem.

00:01:21.650 --> 00:01:33.110
This is fitting because according to Nico
Robin it dates back over 4000 years.

00:01:33.110 --> 00:01:38.540
The capital Arubana to me seems to be based
on this ancient rocky fort in the north west

00:01:38.540 --> 00:01:42.260
of India, that celebrates the Sacred Spirit
Festival.

00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:46.890
The tomb of the kings, the oldest part of
Alabasta, that concealed the poneglyph, is

00:01:46.890 --> 00:01:52.450
the spitting image of the ancient temple of
Edfu, that is famous for the Edfu building

00:01:52.450 --> 00:01:58.650
texts, that contain the history of the ancient
kingdom of Egypt all the way back to the 'Early

00:01:58.650 --> 00:02:01.240
Primeval Age of the Gods'.

00:02:01.240 --> 00:02:04.410
Damn, that's cool, I definitely want to go
there some day.

00:02:04.410 --> 00:02:10.179
And how very fitting for a place that contains
part of the true history of the one piece

00:02:10.179 --> 00:02:14.599
world and its gods.

00:02:14.599 --> 00:02:21.920
You have characters, like Pell and Chaka,
that have Zoan fruits inspired by the sacred

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:24.351
animals of ancient Egypt, a falcon and a chakul.

00:02:24.351 --> 00:02:31.069
The king himself is named Cobra and the main
antagonist is Crocodile, the animals that

00:02:31.069 --> 00:02:36.959
live in the nil river, which is ironic because
he is the one who takes away the countries

00:02:36.959 --> 00:02:38.329
water supplies.

00:02:38.329 --> 00:02:44.890
And yet, what absolutely blew my mind was
that Alabasta OFFICIALLY is inspired by India,

00:02:44.890 --> 00:02:51.709
which, I'm sorry, but I find absolutely ridiculous,
given all its Egyptian influence and it's

00:02:51.709 --> 00:02:57.769
name literally being a pun on the words Arab
and the white stone Alabasta in Japanese.

00:02:57.769 --> 00:03:01.900
But anyways, what's up I'm Manu and in case
you are wondering how I know this, there is

00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:06.150
actually an official travel guide to the one
piece world, that lists a lot of the real

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:12.879
life inspirations for all the fantastic places
we visit, that actually only dropped in 2021

00:03:12.879 --> 00:03:16.799
and that I haven't heard of for some reason
until now.

00:03:16.799 --> 00:03:22.480
I actually was doing research on this topic
myself when I randomly stumbled upon it half-way

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:23.480
through.

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:28.370
I guess if you clicked on this video, you're
as fascinated by the world that Eiichiro Oda,

00:03:28.370 --> 00:03:32.389
the author of one piece, has created, as much
as I am.

00:03:32.389 --> 00:03:37.910
Because building a whole fictional world,
that feels alive and real is actually one

00:03:37.910 --> 00:03:42.260
of the most complex things you can do in story
telling.

00:03:42.260 --> 00:03:48.099
And since no one can create a whole world
out of nothing, naturally – even if only

00:03:48.099 --> 00:03:54.109
subconsciously – you will adapt and incorporate
some real-world elements into your imaginary

00:03:54.109 --> 00:03:59.269
setting and story, using them as a base of
inspiration without copying things 1:1.

00:03:59.269 --> 00:04:04.400
For me, this has two big advantages: One,
It makes your world and your characters feel

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:10.939
familiar to your audience and two, it anchors
your fiction in reality to make it more believable

00:04:10.939 --> 00:04:12.370
and relatable.

00:04:12.370 --> 00:04:17.930
And I think Oda-sensei, who despite barely
leaving his office, is obsessed with learning

00:04:17.930 --> 00:04:23.830
about the history, geography and culture of
the world, has mastered this advanced technique

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:25.770
to a ridiculous level.

00:04:25.770 --> 00:04:32.180
His world of islands and pirates is incredibly
unique and new, but still everything feels

00:04:32.180 --> 00:04:34.340
familiar and coherent.

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:39.479
As I showed you with the example of Alabasta,
he achieves this by taking a number of real

00:04:39.479 --> 00:04:44.669
life inspirations from all over the world
and combines the attributes he likes into

00:04:44.669 --> 00:04:55.270
something completely new.

00:04:55.270 --> 00:05:01.280
So allow me to take you on a tour through
the one piece world and all its fantastic

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:03.830
inspirations - in no particular order.

00:05:03.830 --> 00:05:09.250
Some of these are based on the official book
and others...let's say educated guesses.

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:17.310
And I want to start with Luffy's home, dawn
island in the east blue.

00:05:17.310 --> 00:05:21.800
Now most of the east blue is inspired by asian
places.

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:27.120
Nami's home is inspired by Indonesia, Zoro's
village is inspired by Nara in Japan and the

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:30.790
Baratie is inspired by Vietnam's floating
restaurants.

00:05:30.790 --> 00:05:36.780
This makes sense because it is literally called
the east blue, Asia being in the east.

00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:41.360
And when I looked deeper into this, it actually
seems to be the , direction Oda-sensei went

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:43.919
with the entire one piece world.

00:05:43.919 --> 00:05:48.819
The west blue for instance features, locations
like Ohara, that is based on England, Ballywood

00:05:48.819 --> 00:05:54.210
Kingdom, that is based on Hollywood of course
and thriller bark, that is inspired by French

00:05:54.210 --> 00:05:56.800
gothic architecture like the Notre dam.

00:05:56.800 --> 00:06:02.360
Anyways, the Goa kingdom in the east blue
also falls into this pattern, because it is

00:06:02.360 --> 00:06:06.500
based on the Philippines with it's jungles
and warm climate.

00:06:06.500 --> 00:06:11.449
By the way one of the most beautiful countries
I have been to.

00:06:11.449 --> 00:06:16.900
The rich capital and the grey terminal seem
to be a representation of smokey mountain,

00:06:16.900 --> 00:06:21.910
a giant landfill in Manila, the capital of
the Philippines, where people lived and worked

00:06:21.910 --> 00:06:23.930
in heaps of garbage.

00:06:23.930 --> 00:06:27.880
Just like in One pIece, the landfill experienced
devastating fires.

00:06:27.880 --> 00:06:32.400
In the story, it's the nobles that purposefully
want to get rid of all the poor people living

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:44.860
there to not anger the celestial dragons coming
to visit.

00:06:44.860 --> 00:06:51.469
The capital city itself however seems to be
based on the Indian state of Goa, Indias richest

00:06:51.469 --> 00:06:56.659
region, once again contrasting the striking
gap between rich and poor.

00:06:56.659 --> 00:07:01.159
For Fusha village on the other hand it seems
like Oda-sensei drew inspiration from the

00:07:01.159 --> 00:07:06.610
English country side, once again merging three
very different countries into one.

00:07:06.610 --> 00:07:11.880
I wish I could nerd out a bit more about how
awesome I find this combination, but for your

00:07:11.880 --> 00:07:12.880
sake, let's move on.

00:07:12.880 --> 00:07:17.909
This is the freaky island of Punk hazard,
that not only looks like the worlds largest

00:07:17.909 --> 00:07:31.750
poke ball, but is half Mordor and half North
Pole.

00:07:31.750 --> 00:07:35.469
Basically how my balls feel when I go into
a Japanese onsen in winter.

00:07:35.469 --> 00:07:36.550
Cant recommend enough.

00:07:36.550 --> 00:07:41.639
Well you might or might not be surprised when
I tell you that there is a place like in the

00:07:41.639 --> 00:07:43.180
real world as well.

00:07:43.180 --> 00:07:48.830
Because Iceland is pretty much a song of fire
and ice as well, only that they were smart

00:07:48.830 --> 00:07:51.539
enough to stopp after four seasons.

00:07:51.539 --> 00:07:57.870
With some of the most unreal and epic landscapes
in the world, here hot glowing volcanic lava

00:07:57.870 --> 00:08:02.449
meets icy glaciers with only few inhabitants.

00:08:02.449 --> 00:08:07.639
Similar to how Punk Hazard's conditions have
made it a hard place to live.

00:08:07.639 --> 00:08:18.659
But damn I want to go to Iceland so so badly.

00:08:18.659 --> 00:08:24.180
Now Wano, the longest arc of the entire story,
is of course inspired by Japan.

00:08:24.180 --> 00:08:30.349
However there are so ridiculously many details
from real Japan hidden in this arc, that it

00:08:30.349 --> 00:08:34.900
would probably be an entire video of its own,
so let me know if you want to see that.

00:08:34.900 --> 00:08:41.769
Next we have a place that I have enjoyed talking
about a lot in my videos recently, Drum Island,

00:08:41.769 --> 00:08:44.889
home of chopper.

00:08:44.889 --> 00:08:52.740
The island as a whole, that is always covered
in snow, is mostly based on Northern America

00:08:52.740 --> 00:08:54.690
and the Rocky Mountain region.

00:08:54.690 --> 00:08:59.251
The iconic cone shaped peaks are most likely
inspired by the devils tower in the north

00:08:59.251 --> 00:09:00.320
of Wyoming.

00:09:00.320 --> 00:09:04.430
And yes I cant believe that's a real place
either.

00:09:04.430 --> 00:09:09.980
The town of Cocoa Weed is basically a copy
of the Canadian city Banff.

00:09:09.980 --> 00:09:14.959
However interestingly enough, Big Horn the
town where the straw hats arrive, appears

00:09:14.959 --> 00:09:23.380
to be inspired by the cute city of Alberobello
in Italy.

00:09:23.380 --> 00:09:30.060
Meanwhile, and as a German I can't believe
I missed this, Drum Castle, where Dr. Kureha

00:09:30.060 --> 00:09:36.200
resides, is of course based on the legendary
Neuschwanstein castle in the state of Bavaria,

00:09:36.200 --> 00:09:37.680
where I'm actually from.

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:38.680
How embarrassing.

00:09:38.680 --> 00:09:43.560
Oda-sensei really went out of his way to create
a winter-wonder land here, giving it that

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:45.080
Christmassy vibe.

00:09:45.080 --> 00:09:48.940
Before I go on to the next big one, here are
a few smaller ones.

00:09:48.940 --> 00:09:51.850
Whiskey Peak is inspired by Taos in New Mexico.

00:09:51.850 --> 00:09:55.690
Twin peaks is basically Thacher Island, also
in the US.

00:09:55.690 --> 00:10:01.399
I talked about that in a recent theory about
the one piece being inside a whale like Laboon.

00:10:01.399 --> 00:10:05.899
The castle on top of the red line, Marijois,
from where the Government Rules the world

00:10:05.899 --> 00:10:15.500
is inspired by the, and I'm sorry for slaughtering
this, Chateau de Chambord in France, a 2 hour

00:10:15.500 --> 00:10:22.420
car ride away from Paris.

00:10:22.420 --> 00:10:28.540
Both the real chateau and Marijois have vast
gardens and a pure statement of power and

00:10:28.540 --> 00:10:30.260
luxury.

00:10:30.260 --> 00:10:35.880
Interestingly enough it is closely related
to the French Revolution, where the revolutionary

00:10:35.880 --> 00:10:38.930
army took it away from the governing nobility.

00:10:38.930 --> 00:10:42.510
I wonder if that might become relevant in
the story.

00:10:42.510 --> 00:10:48.060
Zou the giant elephant, is most likely a twist
on the whale with an island on its back trope,

00:10:48.060 --> 00:10:53.639
but I believe Oda-sensei might also have seen
an image of this famous rock that looks like

00:10:53.639 --> 00:10:58.300
an elephant off the coast of Iceland.

00:10:58.300 --> 00:11:05.970
The city of the minks on the other Hand is
inspired by the monument Valley in Yemen.

00:11:05.970 --> 00:11:11.100
There is also this island, called the Rommel
Kingdom, that we see in Cavendish's flashback.

00:11:11.100 --> 00:11:16.810
His alter ego Hakuba is based on the infamous
serial killer, Jack the Ripper, and his hometown

00:11:16.810 --> 00:11:21.360
in general in based on 19th century London.

00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:26.779
And I personally, am inspired by you subscribing
to the channel if you want more one piece

00:11:26.779 --> 00:11:27.821
content like this.

00:11:27.821 --> 00:11:33.279
This is Amazon Lilly, an empire only run by
then women of the Kuja clan, located in the

00:11:33.279 --> 00:11:41.649
calm belt, where Luffy was transported by
Kuma.

00:11:41.649 --> 00:11:46.850
While the women themselves are inspired by
the legendary amazon warriors from greek mythology,

00:11:46.850 --> 00:11:53.240
the island itself is actually inspired by
the so called hanging temple in the north-east

00:11:53.240 --> 00:11:55.800
of china, close the mountains of Mongolia.

00:11:55.800 --> 00:12:02.259
Yes, I know, these look completely unreal,
towering over 30 meters from the ground inside

00:12:02.259 --> 00:12:08.610
that cliff, but they are an actual place,
built over 1500 years ago.

00:12:08.610 --> 00:12:14.940
I love how unique the combination of these
two ideas is, making Amazon Lilly a truly

00:12:14.940 --> 00:12:23.320
spectacular place.

00:12:23.320 --> 00:12:24.330
Then we have Dressrosa.

00:12:24.330 --> 00:12:29.480
You might already know that this island is
heavily inspired by Spain and Spanish culture,

00:12:29.480 --> 00:12:31.610
for example with viola's tango dance.

00:12:31.610 --> 00:12:37.230
The architecture resembles that of the famous
Gaudi, who's influence you can see all over

00:12:37.230 --> 00:12:38.230
Barcelona.

00:12:38.230 --> 00:12:42.459
Park Güell in particular looks a lot like
the buildings we see throughout the country

00:12:42.459 --> 00:12:44.040
under Doflamingo's rule.

00:12:44.040 --> 00:12:48.950
And just how Crocodile was inspired by an
animal that is connected to Egypt, Don Quixote

00:12:48.950 --> 00:12:54.430
Doflamingo himself is a nod to both the flamingos
living in the Spanish salines, but also to

00:12:54.430 --> 00:12:55.430
the dance Flamenco.

00:12:55.430 --> 00:12:59.720
Oh, and of course the famous story of Don
Quixote.

00:12:59.720 --> 00:13:04.910
Oda-sensei actually commented the following
here himself:

00:13:04.910 --> 00:13:08.800
When I took a close look at Doflamingo and
tried to think of what country would suit

00:13:08.800 --> 00:13:09.800
him.

00:13:09.800 --> 00:13:12.310
I arrived at the conclusion that it's Spain.

00:13:12.310 --> 00:13:16.890
I’ve mentioned that the countries of One
Piece are all inspired by real-life countries

00:13:16.890 --> 00:13:21.220
in another SBS before, but it’s the first
time I got feedback from the residents of

00:13:21.220 --> 00:13:22.279
such a country.

00:13:22.279 --> 00:13:26.700
I can’t be irresponsible in the way I draw,
but if you do see anything that seems like

00:13:26.700 --> 00:13:30.889
a half-baked version of your culture or buildings,
please forgive me.

00:13:30.889 --> 00:13:33.050
Remember, it’s just a manga.

00:13:33.050 --> 00:13:37.560
Haha, I wish more people would take that last
sentence to heart.

00:13:37.560 --> 00:13:42.509
The Giant coloseum on the other hand is of
course inspired by the actual colosseum in

00:13:42.509 --> 00:13:45.620
Rome or Ancient Greece.

00:13:45.620 --> 00:13:53.209
Now let's move on to my absolute favourite
location in all of One PIece: Water seven.

00:13:53.209 --> 00:13:57.820
And not only because Enies Lobby and water
seven are my favorite arc, but also because

00:13:57.820 --> 00:14:07.310
the island itself is absolutely breathtaking.

00:14:07.310 --> 00:14:12.509
It's a floating city with canals instead of
streets, that is famous for its shipwrights.

00:14:12.509 --> 00:14:17.680
This city is of course heavily inspired by
Venice, that is also built on the water and

00:14:17.680 --> 00:14:19.199
full with canals.

00:14:19.199 --> 00:14:23.470
The venitians were famous for their ships,
that they used to build a flourishing global

00:14:23.470 --> 00:14:27.540
trading empire, reflected in water sevens
skill with ship building.

00:14:27.540 --> 00:14:35.390
If you ever have the chance to visit Venice,
it's just as breathtaking as it look...maybe

00:14:35.390 --> 00:14:36.839
even more so.

00:14:36.839 --> 00:14:53.070
The masks of Venetian carnival are used incredibly
creatively to introduce the Cypher Pol agencies.

00:14:53.070 --> 00:14:57.060
The building of the galley-la company, that
is run by Franky's step brother Ice Berg,

00:14:57.060 --> 00:15:01.579
is inspired by the piazza dell'anfiteatro
in the Tuscany in northern Italy.

00:15:01.579 --> 00:15:06.930
The only thing that seems to be non-italian
on water seven is it's clear resemblance to

00:15:06.930 --> 00:15:17.779
the island Mont Saint Michael in the normandy
in France, that depending on the tides is

00:15:17.779 --> 00:15:23.639
completely surrounded by water as well and
strongly resembles the shape of water seven.

00:15:23.639 --> 00:15:25.930
But let's go back to Venice for a second.

00:15:25.930 --> 00:15:31.350
Not only is the city slowly sinking into the
ocean every single year, but it frequently

00:15:31.350 --> 00:15:37.870
experiences the so called Acqua Alta, a phenomenon
where the city is flooded by high tides.

00:15:37.870 --> 00:15:44.509
I suspect, that this is the inspiration for
the enormous aqua laguna, a tsunami like wave

00:15:44.509 --> 00:15:56.569
that rolls over water seven every single year
and causes to island to sink a little.

00:15:56.569 --> 00:16:01.829
I can't help but wonder what secrets lie beneath
the surface here as well.

00:16:01.829 --> 00:16:06.449
As you know, I am convinced that there is
a much bigger and deeper secret to this stunning

00:16:06.449 --> 00:16:10.260
world of one piece and why so much of it is
under water.

00:16:10.260 --> 00:16:15.050
For example the connection between the Aqua
Laguna and the going whole under Enies Lobby.

00:16:15.050 --> 00:16:18.420
And what do the devil fruits have to do with
all this?

00:16:18.420 --> 00:16:24.519
One crazy, but very real possibility for example,
is that the devil fruits actually originate

00:16:24.519 --> 00:16:30.889
from a giant tree on Laugh Tale, that is under
the sea just next to water seven.

00:16:30.889 --> 00:16:35.290
And that’s why you really shouldnt ignore
this video, because it will prove to you that

00:16:35.290 --> 00:16:39.760
One Piece's world building goes way deeper
than you could ever dream.

